EXTENSION "ARMDef_Faith_and_Flame_ThePyrenees_VirtuesFlaws" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, Faith & Flame - Chapter Six: The Pyrenees and the Hispanic March virtues flaws"
    VERSION "0.5.1"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-06"
    DEPENDS_ON "ARMDef_Faith_and_Flame_Core_Ext"

    # The chapter's virtues flaws, structured; each DESCRIPTION the source's text, verbatim.

    #t0c9f561a6fe4e57024d904 ^"Faerie Blood: Jentil" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tT28cb9EpHcSa3Joedekm2A3 ^"Virtue"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Printed Kind" STRING "Minor or Major Supernatural Virtue"
            ^"Size" STRING "Major or Minor"
            ^"Category" STRING "Supernatural"
            ^"Source" STRING "Faith & Flame"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 91
        }
        DESCRIPTION "You claim descent from the race of giants who once ruled the lands of the Basque Country. Though now defeated and virtually extinct, your ancestors created enormous stone monuments, and invented both metallurgy and agriculture. Their legacy lives in you. As a Minor Virtue, this grants you a +1 bonus to resist aging, a +1 bonus to recovery rolls, and a +1 increase in Strength, to a maximum of +3. This Virtue is compatible with Large and Giant’s Blood. As a Major Virtue, it grants Second Sight, replaces the bonus to recovery with a +1 increase in Size, and increases the bonus to resist aging to +3 while disregarding aging rolls until age 50. The Major virtue marks you with a distinctive appearance indicating your ancestry, such as oversized hands and feet or exaggerated facial features."
    }

    #tfa3a5294782fd48d613ac0 ^"Faerie Blood: Laminak" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tT28cb9EpHcSa3Joedekm2A3 ^"Virtue"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Printed Kind" STRING "Minor Supernatural Virtue"
            ^"Size" STRING "Minor"
            ^"Category" STRING "Supernatural"
            ^"Source" STRING "Faith & Flame"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 91
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Descended from the river fae of the Basque Country, you favor either their hard-working or beautiful nature. You may add +1 to either your Stamina or Presence, but not to more than +3. Many mortals find you intriguing, but don’t understand why. Characters with this Virtue have webbed toes."
    }

    #t7e2aaa72b92386f66dbded ^"Chthonic Sorginak Magic" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tT28cb9EpHcSa3Joedekm2A3 ^"Virtue"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Printed Kind" STRING "Major, Supernatural"
            ^"Size" STRING "Major"
            ^"Category" STRING "Supernatural"
            ^"Source" STRING "Faith & Flame"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 93
        }
        DESCRIPTION "This grants a variant of the Supernatural Ability of Chthonic Magic beginning at a score of 1. Similar to the Hermetic Virtue, this magic, said to spring from instruction by Mari, grants the sorgina the ability to tap into sinister powers. The sorgina is attuned to both the Magic and Infernal realms. She gains botch dice from neither, and enjoys the benefits of both. She can use Infernal vis without penalty, and adds her Chthonic Magic to her Folk Witch Magic Theory when determining how many pawns of Infernal vis she can use in a season. Neither Faerie nor Magic-aligned detection can sense this tainted Infernal alignment, but Divine and Infernal powers can.\n\nFinally, if she incorporates a knowingly blasphemous action in her magic, the sorgina gains a +6 bonus to the roll or total in question, and she may optionally incorporate Casting Items to also add their Shape & Material bonuses (up to her Folk Witch Magic Theory score). She does not gain the additional Ranges, Targets or Durations ordinarily associated with Chthonic Magic, such as Crossroads, Cursed, or Passion. See *Realms of Power: Infernal*, page 123 for additional details."
    }

    #t08c519fe4df73b8c03256d ^"Ecstatic Magic" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tT28cb9EpHcSa3Joedekm2A3 ^"Virtue"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Printed Kind" STRING "Minor Supernatural Virtue"
            ^"Size" STRING "Minor"
            ^"Category" STRING "Supernatural"
            ^"Source" STRING "Faith & Flame"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 93
        }
        DESCRIPTION "The sorgina gains the ability Ecstatic Magic at 1 and she may stray from her body in an intangible spirit form for one hour during akelarre with a successful Stamina + Ecstatic Magic + stress die roll against an Ease Factor of 12. For every 3 by which the roll exceeds the Ease Factor, the sorgina may stray for an additional hour. While straying, she may move with a Stamina + Athletics roll (Ease Factor 3) to visit places she sees daily. For every 3 the roll exceeds the ease factor, she may travel to places she has seen in the last week (Ease Factor 6), the last year (Ease Factor 9), not been in the last year (Ease Factor 12), and places she has never been but possesses an associated arcane connection (Ease Factor 15). While straying, she has the Second Sight ability equal to her Ecstatic Magic ability. The character manifests any carried accoutrements and may harm spirits in intangible form; spirits may also harm her. She may become tangible with a Stamina + Concentration roll (Ease Factor 12), and may be harmed normally when tangible. She must make an additional roll to remain tangible if wounded; wound penalties apply to the roll."
    }

    #t7ca48dd74d93e69f6cc01c ^"Sorgina" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tT28cb9EpHcSa3Joedekm2A3 ^"Virtue"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Printed Kind" STRING "Free Social Status Virtue"
            ^"Size" STRING "Free"
            ^"Category" STRING "Social Status"
            ^"Source" STRING "Faith & Flame"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 94
        }
        DESCRIPTION "The character is a member of the folk witch tradition of the Pyrenees, with members in Provence and Iberia. Basque villagers respect or fear the character, but members of the Church might persecute a sorgina for heretical behavior. This Virtue is equivalent with the Folk Witch Social Status (See Hedge Magic, page 34) and may be taken in addition to the Hermetic Magus Social Status Virtue. It is also compatible with many other Social Status Virtues and Flaws, and with Wealthy and Poor. The character has been trained as a sorgina. She may perform folk witch laboratory activities such as brewing potions, she uses sorgina casting methods with her Supernatural Virtues and gains the associated magical defenses, and she is a member of a coven who attends akelarre meetings. As she is not supported by a covenant, like a magus is, she must spend two seasons each year supporting herself– normally by performing magical services for the local community. She may not take Virtues and Flaws associated with Witch’s Moon. (*Hedge Magic Revised Edition*, page 42)"
    }

    #ta3ee0698884218eaffdc96 ^"Exotic Casting (Faith & Flame)" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tT28cb9EpHcSa3Joedekm2A3 ^"Virtue"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Printed Kind" STRING "Minor, Hermetic"
            ^"Printed Name" STRING "Exotic Casting"
            ^"Size" STRING "Minor"
            ^"Category" STRING "Hermetic"
            ^"Source" STRING "Faith & Flame"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 98
        }
        DESCRIPTION "The magus uses non-Hermetic methods to cast Hermetic spells. While he still needs to employ obvious ritual actions, these are not the same words and gestures taught as part of Magic Theory within the Order, and other magi who are unfamiliar with the magus’ tradition find it very hard to recognize which spell he is casting. Any attempt to determine the Form of his magical effect (**ArM5**, page 83) is made against an Ease Factor of 15, without the magnitude of the effect being subtracted from this Ease Factor as normal. If the character has any Supernatural Abilities, then he uses the same methods to cast his Hermetic magic as he does to use his non-Hermetic magic. The magus cannot choose to use the standard Hermetic methods instead of those of his native tradition, but can choose to reduce or forgo words and gestures in the usual fashion (**ArM5**, page 83)."
    }

    #t862644de441a58bfc4c7bd ^"Potent Magic (Faith & Flame)" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tT28cb9EpHcSa3Joedekm2A3 ^"Virtue"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Printed Kind" STRING "Minor or Major Hermetic Virtue"
            ^"Printed Name" STRING "Potent Magic"
            ^"Size" STRING "Major or Minor"
            ^"Category" STRING "Hermetic"
            ^"Source" STRING "Faith & Flame"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 96
        }
        DESCRIPTION "The maga’s magic is particularly attuned to a narrow field, much as in a Magical Focus. The benefits of Potent Magic are compatible with a Magical Focus; unlike a Magical Focus, a magus may have more than one area of Potent Magic, though only one Potent Magic Virtue applies to any single activity.\n\nPotent Magic provides the maga with a bonus in her field of magic, and permits her to devise Potent spells which gain a casting bonus from the sympathetic magic in shapes and materials.\n\nPotent Magic can be taught as an alternative to a Magical Focus. For sorginak, it may be taken during character creation."
    }

}
